<title>NETHERLANDS: PHILIPS, FEI AGREE TO COMBINE.</title>
<headline>PHILIPS, FEI AGREE TO COMBINE.</headline>
<dateline>EINDHOVEN, Netherlands 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philips Electronics NV said on Friday it had reached definitive agreement to integrate the activities of Philips Electron Optics with FEI Co of Hillsborough, Oregon.</p>
<p>The companies announced in September that FEI would take over most of the assets of Philips Electron Optics, in return for which Philips would receive a stake of 55 percent in FEI.</p>
<p>The transaction is likely to be concluded by January 1997, Philips said. FEI's shareholders still have to approve the deal.</p>
<p>FEI makes ion beam systems. In 1995 the company made net profits of $3.74 million on revenues of $41.7 million.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
